<.shell title="Member letter" current={:member_letter}>
  <h1>Member letter</h1>
  <p class="lead">A member's tax credit letter for a year.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-md">
    <div class="card side-card">
      <.member_letter
        id="member-letter-demo"
        team={SampleData.sample_team()}
        letter={SampleData.letter()}
        year={2025}
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>The download alone, as Your membership shows it beside this year's numbers:</p>
  <div class="demo max-w-md">
    <div class="card side-card">
      <.member_letter
        id="member-letter-short-demo"
        team={SampleData.sample_team()}
        letter={SampleData.letter()}
        year={2025}
        hours={false}
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>The current year, before a team admin can make its letter:</p>
  <div class="demo max-w-md">
    <div class="card side-card">
      <.member_letter id="member-letter-coming-demo" team={SampleData.sample_team()} year={2026} />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A member's own letter: the latest on Your membership, as the download alone, and the
    year's on the year page with its hours.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>A team admin's list of letters. That is the Tax credit letters table.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>The year, what it is for, then the primary and secondary hours the letter says.</li>
    <li>Download letter is a plain button: the page has no one main action.</li>
    <li>An old letter whose hours did not parse shows no hours.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.member_letter id team letter year&gt;</code>
    from <code>Web.Components.MemberLetter</code>, with the letter or nil, and
    <code>hours={false}</code>
    for the download alone.
  </p>
</.shell>
